From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a3xx: reconcile the ring before suspending an uninitialized GPU

msm_gpu_pm_resume() enables power and marks needs_hw_init. CP
initialization is deferred until the next submit. If another system
suspend happens before that submit, A3xx can compare the reset hardware
RPTR (zero) with the software WPTR from before power collapse. Its idle
check then fails with -EBUSY even though all previous submissions
retired before suspend. SM-T531 reproduces this after repeated display-
off/s2idle cycles: RPTR/WPTR are 0/528, and adreno_system_suspend aborts
the system transition.

When hardware initialization is pending, reconcile the software ring
cursor with the actual hardware WPTR before testing idle. Reading WPTR
rather than assuming zero also covers retained hardware state. Keep the
normal ring-drain, GPU-busy and VBIF-halt checks; no fences or
submitted-job state are reset. An invalid hardware pointer remains an
error. Initialized/active command streams keep the existing path.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a3xx_gpu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a3xx_gpu.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a3xx_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a3xx_gpu.c
@@ -538,6 +538,22 @@ static int a3xx_pm_suspend(struct msm_gpu *gpu)
 {
 	int ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * Resume defers CP initialization until the next submit. A second
+	 * suspend can therefore see reset hardware pointers alongside the
+	 * software cursor from before power collapse. Preserve the real idle
+	 * checks by using the hardware producer position in this state.
+	 */
+	if (gpu->needs_hw_init) {
+		struct msm_ringbuffer *ring = gpu->rb[0];
+		u32 wptr = gpu_read(gpu, REG_AXXX_CP_RB_WPTR);
+
+		if (WARN_ON_ONCE(wptr >= MSM_GPU_RINGBUFFER_SZ / sizeof(u32)))
+			return -EINVAL;
+
+		ring->cur = ring->next = ring->start + wptr;
+	}
+
 	if (!a3xx_idle(gpu))
 		return -EBUSY;
 
